An address applies to the last step of a chain -- both spellings.

TWO BUGS, ONE RULE, AND THE RULE WAS ALREADY WRITTEN DOWN.

postfix_expr_arrow computes `chain_continues` and the comment above it says
exactly the right thing -- "an intermediate `->` or `[` still has to load the
pointer to follow it" -- and then applies it to the prefix ++/-- flag only.
Address_of was left out, so `&` suppressed the load at EVERY arrow:

    &p->ref->type      ldr [p]  add 8  add 8
     p->ref->type.t    ldr [p]  add 8  ldr  add 8  ldr

The middle load is how you follow `->ref`. Without it the second offset lands
on the ADDRESS of ref rather than on what ref points at.

The parenthesised spelling failed differently. primary_expr hands Address_of
into grouping parens, which is right for `&(x)` -- the parenthesised thing IS
the target -- and wrong the moment a chain follows the `)`, because then the
inside is an ordinary value. That one dropped the FIRST load:

    &(p)->ref->type             add 8  ldr  add 8

The lookahead scans to the MATCHING paren, not the next one, because the inside
may contain calls and casts of its own; Address_of is restored afterwards so
the chain still ends in an address.

WHAT IT COST. tcc writes the parenthesised form, because pointed_type is a
macro:

    #define pointed_type(t) (&(t)->ref->type)

compare_types calls it for every pointer comparison, so ANY assignment of a
pointer-valued expression walked a wild address:

    char *p = g();     SIGSEGV
    int   n = g();     fine
    g();               fine, the result is never stored

HOW IT WAS FOUND, because the method is the point. tcctest.c had been failing
at line 293 locally for many rounds and was skipped over as "the native crash
is the real one". It is not: 293 is `const char *fn = get_file_from_header();`
-- a pointer-valued call assigned to a variable, reproducible in the sandbox in
one second. Function-ENTRY instrumentation over all 212 functions of tccgen.c
then printed the path directly:

    vstore -> verify_assign_cast -> is_null_pointer -> is_integer_btype
           -> compare_types -> is_compatible_unqualified_types -> compare_types

and compare_types' pointer branch is two lines long.

FIFTH FUNCTION, AND CASE 44 CAME WITH IT. zzc taught this rule to the prefix
operators, zzg to the dot site, zzm to the array site. Closing these two also
closed case 44 -- `&((*p)->m)`, open since the beginning of the spike --
without touching it. Three spellings of one bug, which is the strongest
argument yet that the rule belongs in one place instead of five.

MEASURED

    difftest      73 pass / 0 fail / 0 known gap, amd64  (1 arch-skipped)
                  74 pass / 0 fail / 0 known gap, aarch64
                  the first run of this suite with NO known gap
    corpus        423 of 426 on aarch64
    vocabulary    clean on five architectures
    mc-tcc        char *p = g();   crash -> exit 0
                  tcctest.c        line 294 -> line 337

